title: "NeuroCore: A General Computational Architecture for Dynamic Systems Analysis and Structural Invariance Research"

version: "1.5.0"
date-released: "2026-06-04"

abstract: >
  NeuroCore is an experimental computational research architecture
  designed to investigate dynamic organization, structural invariance,
  functional stability, state transitions, resilience and temporal
  evolution across heterogeneous systems.

  Its methodological scope is not restricted to a predefined
  scientific or application domain. The architecture provides
  computational methods for the analysis of temporal dynamics,
  structural relationships, cross-dataset consistency and
  comparative system behavior.

  Potential extensions include biological, physiological,
  mechanical, computational, informational and semantic systems,
  subject to the availability of appropriate representations,
  operational definitions and independent empirical validation.

  NeuroCore aims to investigate whether common computational
  signatures and organizational properties can be identified
  across systems with different underlying structures and
  representations.

  The generality, transferability and empirical validity of
  the proposed methods remain open research questions.

